1. HELM TEMPLATE BASICS
-----------------------
  {{ .Values.replicaCount }}          value from values.yaml
  {{ .Release.Name }}                 release name
  {{ .Chart.Name }} {{ .Chart.AppVersion }}
  {{ .Values.image.repository }}:{{ .Values.image.tag | default .Chart.AppVersion }}
  {{- ... }} / {{ ... -}}             trim whitespace
  {{ include "mychart.fullname" . }}  call a helper from _helpers.tpl
  {{ toYaml .Values.resources | nindent 12 }}   insert a YAML block
  {{- if .Values.ingress.enabled }} ... {{- end }}
  {{- range .Values.env }} ... {{- end }}
  {{ .Values.name | quote }}  {{ required "image.repository is required" .Values.image.repository }}

Config-change rollouts (Day 22 problem solved):
  annotations:
    checksum/config: {{ include (print $.Template.BasePath "/configmap.yaml") . | sha256sum }}

Test and lint:
  helm lint ./mychart
  helm template x ./mychart -f values-prod.yaml
  helm install x ./mychart --dry-run=server


2. KUSTOMIZE
------------
Built into kubectl (k apply -k). NO templates: plain YAML + patches.
  base/
    kustomization.yaml   resources: [deployment.yaml, service.yaml]
    deployment.yaml
    service.yaml
  overlays/
    dev/kustomization.yaml    resources: [../../base] + patches
    prod/kustomization.yaml

Common fields:
  namespace: prod
  namePrefix: prod-
  labels: [...] / commonLabels
  images:                         # change image tag without editing YAML
  - name: myapp
    newName: docker.io/me/myapp
    newTag: v5
  replicas:
  - name: myapp
    count: 4
  configMapGenerator:             # generates ConfigMap with hash suffix
  - name: app-config              # -> name changes when content changes
    literals: [LOG_LEVEL=info]    # -> automatic rollout!
  patches:
  - path: patch-resources.yaml

  k kustomize overlays/prod      render
  k apply -k overlays/prod       apply


3. HELM vs KUSTOMIZE
--------------------
                 Helm                           Kustomize
  Style          templates + values             overlays + patches
  Packaging      versioned charts, repos        just folders in Git
  Lifecycle      releases, history, rollback    plain apply (GitOps)
  Best for       distributing software,         your own apps, small
                 many config knobs              env differences
Many teams: Helm for third-party software, Kustomize (or Helm) for
their own apps. Argo CD supports both (Day 54).


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- Helm: values + templates; lint, template, dry-run.
- Kustomize: base + overlays; images and configMapGenerator are the
  most useful features.
- Both render to plain YAML.
